; TEST: abort=1
;
; shl u8 1 by 8: a count equal to the width.
; Abort kind 1, the numeric trap (prelude/README.md) -- the shared
; `bfausr_trap`. If nothing traps the function returns 7.
;
; A count >= N traps (spec 5.4 as amended: "a count >= the width traps, as
; `+` traps on overflow"; ssa-ir.md 2.3). The hardware would mask the count
; (x86 takes cl mod 64, so this would be 256, normalised to 0) -- the target-dependent answer the trap exists to refuse.
; emit.inc compares the count UNSIGNED (`cmp rcx, N` / `jae bfausr_trap`)
; before the shift; the same kind as `+`. N - 1 does not trap:
; shift_narrow.ir.
;
; Mutation (run): the count check dropped -> exit 7.

functio @initium (ptr) -> u8 {
b0:
%0 = param ptr 0
%1 = iconst u8 1
%2 = iconst u8 8
%3 = shl u8 %1 %2
%4 = iconst u8 7
ret %4
}
